theSouthern Sun

252
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:39,086
in figures five-millennium,

253
00:10:39,121 --> 00:10:41,364
and your docking bay 
is one-niner. Over.

254
00:10:41,399 --> 00:10:43,643
-Yeah. 
-Roger.

255
00:10:43,677 --> 00:10:45,472
ShuttleLancer locked to 
guidance control.

256
00:10:45,506 --> 00:10:46,646
Over.

257
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:47,785
-[Humming "On the Beautiful
Blue Danube"]

258
00:10:47,819 --> 00:10:50,788
♪ Lame, bum bum, lame, lame

259
00:10:50,822 --> 00:10:54,343
-Shuttle craft determined to be
cute, sir.

260
00:10:56,897 --> 00:11:00,176
[Beep] 
-Shuttle landing successful.

261
00:11:00,211 --> 00:11:02,316
Bellerian survivors 
disembarking.

262
00:11:02,351 --> 00:11:04,767
-Attention all hands.
-Attention.

263
00:11:04,802 --> 00:11:06,769
-Shuttle landing complete.

264
00:11:06,804 --> 00:11:09,703
Prepare for incoming 
Stingray Viper squadron.

265
00:11:09,738 --> 00:11:12,775
-Red 2,Southern Sun in sight.

266
00:11:12,810 --> 00:11:14,639
-Excuse me.

267
00:11:14,674 --> 00:11:16,710
Excuse me. 
-Attention: All those

268
00:11:16,745 --> 00:11:19,437
wishing to meet 
the incoming Viper squadron,

269
00:11:19,471 --> 00:11:21,473
proceed to the docking bay.
-What is that?

270
00:11:21,508 --> 00:11:22,854
-Lea!
-Hi, Dad.

271
00:11:22,889 --> 00:11:24,994
Hi, Scott.
-Hi.

272
00:11:25,029 --> 00:11:26,651
-Ah, so pretty.
-If you're going down to

273
00:11:26,686 --> 00:11:28,653
the docking bay to meet your
friend from Coriolis,

274
00:11:28,688 --> 00:11:29,654
you better hurry.
-Oi!

275
00:11:29,689 --> 00:11:31,138
-The Viperis on final approach.

276
00:11:31,173 --> 00:11:33,244
-Well, I came down to check thathe's on the flight.

277
00:11:33,278 --> 00:11:35,591
-Lieutenant Lemont.

278
00:11:35,625 --> 00:11:37,869
-Mac?
-Contact the pilot

279
00:11:37,904 --> 00:11:41,424
of the Stingray Viperand ask if
Professor Spooner is aboard.

280
00:11:41,459 --> 00:11:43,288
-I'm insane!
-Thank you.

281
00:11:43,323 --> 00:11:46,567
-Sun control, I have a request.

282
00:11:46,602 --> 00:11:48,190
Do you have a Professor Spooner
on board?

283
00:11:48,224 --> 00:11:50,123
Over. 
-Stingray to Sun control.

284
00:11:50,157 --> 00:11:51,572
Affirmative. Over.

285
00:11:51,607 --> 00:11:53,505
-Sting, Debbie Reynolds and God.

286
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:54,990
-Bye, Dad.
-Bye, bye.

287
00:11:55,024 --> 00:11:56,474
-Bye, Scott.
-Bye.

288
00:11:56,508 --> 00:11:58,303
-Southern Sun, we are starting 
our landing sequence.

289
00:11:58,338 --> 00:12:01,721
-In the future, geese will be
rocket-powered.

290
00:12:01,755 --> 00:12:03,239
-Southern Sun, abort landing.

291
00:12:03,274 --> 00:12:04,896
We have birds coming up fast on our tails.

292
00:12:04,931 --> 00:12:08,555
Stingray Two toStingray Three, 
we are under fire.

293
00:12:08,589 --> 00:12:10,143
Prepare for defense formation.

294
00:12:10,177 --> 00:12:12,766
-Roger,Stingray Two.
-Graphics by Kenner.

295
00:12:12,801 --> 00:12:16,149
-Stingray One, 
assuming defense formation.

296
00:12:16,183 --> 00:12:19,186
We'll cover for you 
and the professor.

297
00:12:19,221 --> 00:12:21,016
-What the hell is going on
out there?

298
00:12:21,050 --> 00:12:22,638
-Look out,Red Three!

299
00:12:22,672 --> 00:12:25,606
-Red Three is down.-I never liked Red Three anyway.

300
00:12:25,641 --> 00:12:27,022
-Damn it!

301
00:12:27,056 --> 00:12:30,094
[Weapons firing]

302
00:12:30,128 --> 00:12:33,683
-♪ Ta da da da -- crap! 
-Pirate ship eliminated.

303
00:12:33,718 --> 00:12:37,377
-Special effects by
Industrial Light and Morons.

304
00:12:37,411 --> 00:12:40,656
♪♪

305
00:12:40,690 --> 00:12:42,313
-Good shot, Ryder!

306
00:12:42,347 --> 00:12:44,453
-Are we the good guys
or the bad guys?

307
00:12:44,487 --> 00:12:46,973
-Attention, all hands: 
Man your battle stations.

308
00:12:47,007 --> 00:12:49,009
We're under attack.

309
00:12:49,044 --> 00:12:51,598
-Uh-oh, an air show.
Look out below!

310
00:12:51,632 --> 00:12:54,325
[Weapons firing]

311
00:12:54,359 --> 00:12:56,603
-Hey, I told you we should have
landed at LaGuardia.

312
00:12:56,637 --> 00:12:59,295
♪♪

313
00:12:59,330 --> 00:13:02,436
Tell me about it --
these briefs I'm wearing, huh?

314
00:13:02,471 --> 00:13:05,715
-So their spaceship
is a huge basement.

315
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:08,339
-Hmm, hmm, hmm, hmm.

316
00:13:08,373 --> 00:13:09,927
Say!

317
00:13:09,961 --> 00:13:11,756
-Commander Kalgan, 
can I help you?

318
00:13:11,791 --> 00:13:14,276
-Calgon? 
-Excuse me, sir.

319
00:13:14,310 --> 00:13:16,692
-Did you have a reservation?

320
00:13:16,726 --> 00:13:19,729
-Commander, sir, 
what are you doing?!

321
00:13:19,764 --> 00:13:22,042
[Beeps twice]

322
00:13:22,077 --> 00:13:24,424
-The hostess will seat you
in a moment, s-- sir!

323
00:13:24,458 --> 00:13:28,255
We have a perfectly fine bar if
you'd like to wait there.

324
00:13:28,290 --> 00:13:30,533
Oh.
Oh, I see.

325
00:13:30,568 --> 00:13:32,294
Oh -- oh, great.
Yeah, shooting me

326
00:13:32,328 --> 00:13:34,779
is not going to get you to
a table any faster, sir.

327
00:13:34,814 --> 00:13:36,608
[Fires]

328
00:13:36,643 --> 00:13:38,265
-I'll get the manager.

329
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:40,578
-Kalgan, blow me away.

330
00:13:40,612 --> 00:13:46,101
♪♪

331
00:13:47,171 --> 00:13:51,140
-Does that guy inflate his pants
to attract mates?

332
00:13:51,175 --> 00:13:53,729
[Explosions]

333
00:13:53,763 --> 00:13:57,491
-Good work.
You blew up the septic tank.

334
00:13:57,526 --> 00:14:00,011
-Well, I don't know, I just
tried to open my garage door.

335
00:14:00,046 --> 00:14:02,807
What the...

336
00:14:02,842 --> 00:14:05,637
-Warning: system power loss.

337
00:14:05,672 --> 00:14:07,294
-Too right!

338
00:14:07,329 --> 00:14:09,124
-Energize our
emergency landing strobe.

339
00:14:09,158 --> 00:14:10,608
-We're off circuit!

340
00:14:10,642 --> 00:14:11,885
It's dead, sir.

341
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:14,060
-Life system failing.

342
00:14:14,094 --> 00:14:15,337
[Beeping]

343
00:14:15,371 --> 00:14:16,648
-We lost power!

344
00:14:16,683 --> 00:14:18,927
-Relax!
You're in your own room.

345
00:14:18,961 --> 00:14:20,376
-We lost power!

346
00:14:20,411 --> 00:14:23,207
♪♪

347
00:14:23,241 --> 00:14:25,795
-Uh, is it a good idea for
a pilot to eject in space?

348
00:14:25,830 --> 00:14:27,245
-Viper out of control. 
Collision imminent.

349
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:30,593
Pilot emergency beam-down 
ejection system activated.

350
00:14:30,628 --> 00:14:33,631
-Attention, all hands: 
prepare for crash landing.

351
00:14:35,012 --> 00:14:37,877
-So really, how does this help
the Basque separatists?

352
00:14:37,911 --> 00:14:39,188
[Man screams]
-Scott!

353
00:14:39,223 --> 00:14:41,397
-My stair stepper.

354
00:14:41,432 --> 00:14:43,779
-Attention: pilot beam-down 
successful.

355
00:14:43,813 --> 00:14:46,782
Medical team, stand by. 
Fire control to docking bay.

356
00:14:46,816 --> 00:14:49,164
-[Snickering]

357
00:14:49,198 --> 00:14:50,993
-Look out!
It's going to blow!

358
00:14:51,028 --> 00:14:53,478
Move!
It's going to blow!

359
00:14:53,513 --> 00:14:55,204
-If the first 10 minutes
are any indication,

360
00:14:55,239 --> 00:14:57,966
this movie is
going to blow!

361
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,416
-My "Buns of Steel" videos
are in there!

362
00:15:00,451 --> 00:15:02,280
-We don't have time!

363
00:15:02,315 --> 00:15:03,316
It's gonna blow!

364
00:15:03,350 --> 00:15:05,628
-But he'll burn alive!

365
00:15:05,663 --> 00:15:08,010
-It's gonna blow!
-Come on, Mother.

366
00:15:08,045 --> 00:15:12,670
[Explosion]

367
00:15:12,704 --> 00:15:16,674
-Oh, yeah, that will take care
of it.

368
00:15:16,708 --> 00:15:19,953
-My God, the professor.

369
00:15:19,988 --> 00:15:21,886
-[Laughs]

370
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:23,370
-[Laughing]

371
00:15:23,405 --> 00:15:25,407
-Remember Carl's blond joke?

372
00:15:25,441 --> 00:15:28,065
-[Evil laughter]

373
00:15:28,099 --> 00:15:29,859
-What happened, lieutenant?

374
00:15:29,894 --> 00:15:31,827
-The Viperwas locked into
the Sun'sguidance control,

375
00:15:31,861 --> 00:15:33,311
commander, and we lost power.

376
00:15:33,346 --> 00:15:35,900
-Commander, the energizing
turbines have been sabotaged.

377
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:37,522
-Sabotaged?

378
00:15:37,557 --> 00:15:40,940
-But what of the little childrenand their toys?

379
00:15:40,974 --> 00:15:42,665
-John Waters!

380
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:44,012
[Beep] 
-Headquarter.

381
00:15:44,046 --> 00:15:46,566
-Blake here.
Give me Kalgan.

382
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:47,670
-Blake. 
-He's right here. Go ahead.

383
00:15:47,705 --> 00:15:49,327
-Blake. 
-Sir, I just saw something

384
00:15:49,362 --> 00:15:50,950
I thought 
you should know about.

385
00:15:50,984 --> 00:15:53,780
-Some strange women came on
board with the Lancer.

386
00:15:53,814 --> 00:15:55,713
-Huh, strange women.
-I'm sorry the information

387
00:15:55,747 --> 00:15:57,784
is so scanty, but I'll send you
up more as I get it.

388
00:15:57,818 --> 00:15:59,751
-Scanty?
-Blake out.

389
00:15:59,786 --> 00:16:01,201
-Hey, look at this.

390
00:16:01,236 --> 00:16:06,034
The office newsletter says I
look like Susan Powter.

391
00:16:06,068 --> 00:16:08,001
-Santa is playing FreeCell
over here.

392
00:16:08,036 --> 00:16:11,142
[Beeping, chiming]

393
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:15,733
-Oh, man, what'd I do?

394
00:16:15,767 --> 00:16:17,321
-What do you think, Devers?

395
00:16:17,355 --> 00:16:18,874
-Should I spend 20 bucks
for Griffey?

396
00:16:18,908 --> 00:16:22,291
-I think whoever did this knows
his way around spaceships.

397
00:16:22,326 --> 00:16:23,672
-I agree.

398
00:16:23,706 --> 00:16:25,881
-I don't know if this helps,
but ho, ho, ho.

399
00:16:25,915 --> 00:16:28,332
-One thing is for sure --
we've got to reduce speed

400
00:16:28,366 --> 00:16:30,265
drastically until we repair
the damage.

401
00:16:30,299 --> 00:16:34,786
You know, I'm thinking more
about the possible motive.

402
00:16:34,821 --> 00:16:36,305
Why?

403
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:37,893
-Commander?

404
00:16:37,927 --> 00:16:39,481
-Ho, ho.

405
00:16:39,515 --> 00:16:43,416
-You get a computer readout on
the damage in the docking bay,

406
00:16:43,450 --> 00:16:46,005
also the pirate fleet's
position, and load the file

407
00:16:46,039 --> 00:16:47,558
into the computer.

408
00:16:47,592 --> 00:16:50,457
I'd like to do some research
on our new female guests,

409
00:16:50,492 --> 00:16:52,356
the Bellerians.
-Nude research.

410
00:16:52,390 --> 00:16:54,289
-I want that ready as soon
as possible.

411
00:16:54,323 --> 00:16:57,913
-Aye, aye, sir.
-Thank you, Devers.

412
00:16:57,947 --> 00:17:01,054
[Synthesized choral music]

413
00:17:01,089 --> 00:17:03,608
-So, uh, we got some
Benedictine monks

414
00:17:03,643 --> 00:17:05,886
in the floorboards,
unfortunately.

415
00:17:05,921 --> 00:17:08,820
We have set some traps with
fresh bread and brandy though.

416
00:17:08,855 --> 00:17:10,995
♪♪

417
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:15,344
-Ladies, this is your new home.

418
00:17:15,379 --> 00:17:18,071
I know it doesn't
look like much,

419
00:17:18,106 --> 00:17:19,521
but if you'll bear with us,

420
00:17:19,555 --> 00:17:22,455
I'm sure we can make you
quite comfortable.

421
00:17:22,489 --> 00:17:26,148
-Leave. We Bellerians wish to 
be alone.

422
00:17:26,183 --> 00:17:28,288
This place will serve 
our purpose.

423
00:17:28,323 --> 00:17:30,118
Leave.

424
00:17:30,152 --> 00:17:31,671
-Whoa, drank too much Surge.

425
00:17:31,705 --> 00:17:34,225
Woo!

426
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:36,469
-Bryce, you okay?

427
00:17:36,503 --> 00:17:39,196
-It's a pleasure having
you onboard.

428
00:17:39,230 --> 00:17:41,060
-I guess.
-Gentlemen.

429
00:17:41,094 --> 00:17:44,718
-Oh, and, uh, by the way,
ladies, there's a ferret cage

430
00:17:44,753 --> 00:17:46,548
by the wall if you need it.

431
00:17:46,582 --> 00:17:50,793
♪♪

432
00:17:50,828 --> 00:17:52,761
-Well, I polished
the back corridor.

433
00:17:52,795 --> 00:17:54,694
Anyone else need
their room done?

434
00:17:58,353 --> 00:18:01,563
-Hey, you guys, I got my dad's
Enforcer for the weekend.

435
00:18:01,597 --> 00:18:03,289
[Man laughing]

436
00:18:03,323 --> 00:18:05,222
-Oh, we have fun, huh?

437
00:18:08,535 --> 00:18:10,917
-Uh, can you help me
out of this thing?

438
00:18:13,126 --> 00:18:15,404
-Our timing was perfect.

439
00:18:15,439 --> 00:18:16,647
Two for the price of one.

440
00:18:16,681 --> 00:18:19,132
-We had a coupon.

441
00:18:19,167 --> 00:18:21,548
-Who'd have thought that
one small spacecraft...

442
00:18:21,583 --> 00:18:23,688
-Robbie Robertson.

443
00:18:23,723 --> 00:18:26,035
-...could have done
that much damage.

444
00:18:26,070 --> 00:18:27,554
-That Viper'smissile pod
took out

445
00:18:27,589 --> 00:18:30,488
the entire winching system
for the docking bay doors.

446
00:18:30,523 --> 00:18:33,457
-Man, you should
have been there.

447
00:18:33,491 --> 00:18:35,631
-According to the damage reports

448
00:18:35,666 --> 00:18:38,220
from the chief
maintenance engineer,

449
00:18:38,255 --> 00:18:40,188
it'll take at least
two weeks

450
00:18:40,222 --> 00:18:42,914
before the docking bay
could be used again.

451
00:18:42,949 --> 00:18:44,088
-I know, it's great.

452
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:45,503
-We couldn't have wished
for it better.

453
00:18:45,538 --> 00:18:46,815
-Yeah.

454
00:18:46,849 --> 00:18:48,230
-That means the Southern Sun

455
00:18:48,265 --> 00:18:51,371
is completely isolated.
-[Stifled snickers]

456
00:18:51,406 --> 00:18:54,167
Nobody can enter her...

457
00:18:54,202 --> 00:18:57,066
and more important,

458
00:18:57,101 --> 00:18:59,793
nobody can leave her.
-[Snickering]

459
00:18:59,828 --> 00:19:01,416
-Excellent.

460
00:19:01,450 --> 00:19:04,384
They no longer have a choice.
[Laughs]

461
00:19:04,419 --> 00:19:06,559
-God, you look good.
Mm.

462
00:19:06,593 --> 00:19:10,321
-It was cruel fate
to be born in space,

463
00:19:10,356 --> 00:19:12,841
but I have vowed
we will not die here.

464
00:19:12,875 --> 00:19:16,189
It is my destiny to set my feet
upon a real world,

465
00:19:16,224 --> 00:19:18,364
and to accumulate wealth
and power

466
00:19:18,398 --> 00:19:21,505
beyond our wildest dreams.

467
00:19:21,539 --> 00:19:24,163
I have offered the people of
the Southern Sun

468
00:19:24,197 --> 00:19:26,234
a rich new life...

469
00:19:26,268 --> 00:19:27,304
-That's good.

470
00:19:27,338 --> 00:19:28,857
-...and now they have
no alternative

471
00:19:28,891 --> 00:19:31,446
but to accept my generosity

472
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:34,621
and alter course
for Corona Borealis.

473
00:19:34,656 --> 00:19:38,315
-Ooh! Don't you love it?!
Ha-ha!

474
00:19:38,349 --> 00:19:40,109
You know, we're always laughing,you and me.

475
00:19:40,144 --> 00:19:41,490
It's great.
-Lieutenant?

476
00:19:41,525 --> 00:19:42,836
-Oi.
-What's the report

477
00:19:42,871 --> 00:19:43,975
from damage control?

478
00:19:44,010 --> 00:19:45,632
-It's not complete yet,
Captain,

479
00:19:45,667 --> 00:19:48,670
but the first reports indicate
that two of our

480
00:19:48,704 --> 00:19:51,776
LM 5,000 X run drive motors
have been sabotaged.

481
00:19:51,811 --> 00:19:52,812
-Boy.

482
00:19:52,846 --> 00:19:54,296
-This also affects
the performance

483
00:19:54,331 --> 00:19:56,712
of one of our Vix
impulse drive generators.

484
00:19:56,747 --> 00:19:58,818
-Oi.
-Give me a computer readout

485
00:19:58,852 --> 00:20:00,060
on our whole stray spectrum.

486
00:20:00,095 --> 00:20:03,685
-Sir.
-Reduce speed by two thirds.

487
00:20:03,719 --> 00:20:05,652
shut down two
of our booster engines.

488
00:20:05,687 --> 00:20:08,034
-Yes, sir.
-Oh, one other thing.

489
00:20:08,068 --> 00:20:09,311
-Oi.
-Can you establish

490
00:20:09,346 --> 00:20:11,727
video contact
with the docking bay?

491
00:20:11,762 --> 00:20:13,488
-Uh, one of the missiles
from the Viper

492
00:20:13,522 --> 00:20:16,387
took out the video
control tower down there,

493
00:20:16,422 --> 00:20:18,527
but we are trying
to reestablish contact

494
00:20:18,562 --> 00:20:20,943
with a Sarid video robot.

495
00:20:20,978 --> 00:20:22,945
-Did you sign Sherry's
birthday card?

496
00:20:25,258 --> 00:20:27,778
-We've been in space too long!

497
00:20:27,812 --> 00:20:30,815
Let us land the ship.
We can do it.

498
00:20:30,850 --> 00:20:32,886
We have the power.
-It's true!

499
00:20:32,921 --> 00:20:34,336
We have the power to do this.

500
00:20:34,371 --> 00:20:35,682
-Yes.
-Yes.

501
00:20:35,717 --> 00:20:37,305
-But this would directly oppose
the law of the Universe.

502
00:20:37,339 --> 00:20:39,203
-Yes.
-The law of the galaxy.

503
00:20:39,238 --> 00:20:40,446
-Forget the law.

504
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:42,448
-No, no, the law
must be upheld.

505
00:20:42,482 --> 00:20:43,759
We cannot break it!

506
00:20:43,794 --> 00:20:45,174
-Oh, yes we can.

507
00:20:45,209 --> 00:20:50,179
-Gentlemen, it seems that
we are not all in agreement.

508
00:20:50,214 --> 00:20:52,389
-I disagree!

509
00:20:52,423 --> 00:20:55,357
-Engineer Parsons seems content
to spend

510
00:20:55,392 --> 00:20:58,326
his remaining years
upon the Southern Sun.

511
00:20:58,360 --> 00:21:00,431
-Then let him do so alone.

512
00:21:00,466 --> 00:21:02,330
-Yeah!
-That's right.

513
00:21:02,364 --> 00:21:03,986
-This is mutiny!
This is treason!

514
00:21:04,021 --> 00:21:05,540
Which I warn you I must report.

515
00:21:05,574 --> 00:21:07,300
-I just have
to wet myself first.

516
00:21:07,335 --> 00:21:12,823
-Will you allow him to spoil
your ambitions

517
00:21:12,857 --> 00:21:14,376
for a greater future?

518
00:21:14,411 --> 00:21:15,791
-I will not allow that, no!

519
00:21:15,826 --> 00:21:18,207
-An easily led wise council.

520
00:21:18,242 --> 00:21:19,485
-No! Traitor!

521
00:21:19,519 --> 00:21:20,589
-What I meant was,

522
00:21:20,624 --> 00:21:22,246
"I totally
endorse what you're doing,"

523
00:21:22,281 --> 00:21:24,766
and g-- ow.
-Rip his band uniform!

524
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,319
Then he'll have to pay for it!

525
00:21:26,354 --> 00:21:28,701
-Oh, next they're going to give
him books so they can dump him.

526
00:21:28,735 --> 00:21:30,806
-Okay.
-Right over here.

527
00:21:30,841 --> 00:21:33,084
-Death by snicker-snag.

528
00:21:33,119 --> 00:21:37,330
♪♪

529
00:21:37,365 --> 00:21:40,471
-I'm going to inflate him
to 35 pounds.

530
00:21:42,853 --> 00:21:45,442
-Okay, then, moving on
to number three on our agenda,

531
00:21:45,476 --> 00:21:46,788
Sherry's birthday party.

532
00:21:46,822 --> 00:21:48,859
-Are they any other of you

533
00:21:48,893 --> 00:21:52,690
that wish to confuse freedom
with treason?

534
00:21:52,725 --> 00:21:55,866
-I'd like to confuse bok choy
with cabbage, sir.

535
00:21:55,900 --> 00:21:57,868
-Report to the Enforcer's
bridge.

536
00:21:57,902 --> 00:21:59,421
-Let's go.
-Hurry up.

537
00:21:59,456 --> 00:22:00,491
-Well, it is the rare meeting

538
00:22:00,526 --> 00:22:02,251
where something
actually got done.

539
00:22:02,286 --> 00:22:03,494
-Mm-hmm.

540
00:22:03,529 --> 00:22:05,116
-You're strict, sir.

541
00:22:05,151 --> 00:22:06,946
-You have done well.

542
00:22:06,980 --> 00:22:10,777
[Whirring, clanking]

543
00:22:21,547 --> 00:22:23,756
-Alone at last.

544
00:22:24,653 --> 00:22:27,242
[Humming]

545
00:22:33,800 --> 00:22:40,324
[Light classical music playing]

546
00:22:40,359 --> 00:22:47,124
♪♪

547
00:22:47,158 --> 00:22:53,889
♪♪

548
00:22:53,924 --> 00:23:00,758
♪♪

549
00:23:00,793 --> 00:23:02,691
Oh!
What the hell?

550
00:23:02,726 --> 00:23:05,798
-Red Norvo, Red Norvo, 
this is Goldilocks Niner.

551
00:23:05,832 --> 00:23:08,697
I'm coming in, sucker. 
Prepare to die.

552
00:23:08,732 --> 00:23:12,080
-Oh, yeah? 
Well, come get some.

553
00:23:12,114 --> 00:23:15,739
-Whoa! Crow, Servo, what the
Hell, Michigan, is going on?

554
00:23:15,773 --> 00:23:17,050
-I can't talk now, Mike.

555
00:23:17,085 --> 00:23:19,570
I'm locked in a death 
struggle with Servo.

556
00:23:19,605 --> 00:23:22,815
-Yeah, me too, Mike, 
only with Crow. Over.

557
00:23:22,849 --> 00:23:25,024
-Cambot, give me rocket
number nine, will you?

558
00:23:25,058 --> 00:23:26,957
-Eat death, Servo!

559
00:23:26,991 --> 00:23:30,063
-Eat munchy crunchy 
chocolaty cocoa death, Crow!

560
00:23:30,098 --> 00:23:33,377
-Enjoy a nice serving of 
Brown Betty with death, but --

561
00:23:33,412 --> 00:23:35,310
but -- but mostly eat death.

562
00:23:38,037 --> 00:23:40,798
-Crow, Servo, you guys
be careful out there.

563
00:23:40,833 --> 00:23:42,973
-Oh, we won't.
[Laughs]

564
00:23:43,007 --> 00:23:44,492
Oh! Ah!

565
00:23:44,526 --> 00:23:46,942
Servo, you just ripped a hole 
in my torso!

566
00:23:46,977 --> 00:23:48,496
Wee!

567
00:23:48,530 --> 00:23:50,877
-Oh! Ah! 
Too late for me!

568
00:23:50,912 --> 00:23:52,534
I took a laser blast 
to the dome.

569
00:23:52,569 --> 00:23:55,088
Wa-hoo!
-Fellas?

570
00:23:55,123 --> 00:23:57,056
-Well, shall we auger 
these babies in?

571
00:23:57,090 --> 00:23:59,196
-After you.

572
00:23:59,230 --> 00:24:01,163
-I love you, Crow!

573
00:24:01,198 --> 00:24:05,029
-I'm sort of fond 
of you, Servo!

574
00:24:05,064 --> 00:24:08,964
[Explosion]

575
00:24:08,999 --> 00:24:11,829
-Crow? Servo?
You -- you guys okay?

576
00:24:14,073 --> 00:24:15,764
Fellas?

577
00:24:22,426 --> 00:24:25,325
Okay, now this
isn't funny anymore.

578
00:24:25,360 --> 00:24:27,120
-Whoa!
-Oh, lighten up, Nelson.

579
00:24:27,155 --> 00:24:28,294
We're robots, remember?

580
00:24:28,328 --> 00:24:29,882
-Man, that was great.
-Yeah.

581
00:24:29,916 --> 00:24:31,642
-So where'd you get
the spaceships?

582
00:24:31,677 --> 00:24:33,782
-Oh, you mean the hyper-warp
escape shuttles

583
00:24:33,817 --> 00:24:35,335
which we just trashed?

584
00:24:35,370 --> 00:24:36,440
-Yeah.
-Oh, they've been down

585
00:24:36,475 --> 00:24:37,683
in the hold
waiting for us to use them

586
00:24:37,717 --> 00:24:39,408
to escape and stuff like that.

587
00:24:39,443 --> 00:24:41,134
-Oh, I see, so don't you think

588
00:24:41,169 --> 00:24:43,723
we maybe should have used them
for escape purposes?!

589
00:24:43,758 --> 00:24:45,691
-Uh, what's he on about?
-What purposes are that?

590
00:24:45,725 --> 00:24:47,658
-Oh, you mean escape from here!

591
00:24:47,693 --> 00:24:48,763
-Oh!
-Aw, geez!

592
00:24:48,797 --> 00:24:50,040
How stupid of us, Mike!

593
00:24:50,074 --> 00:24:52,352
Man!
-Boy, is my face red.

594
00:24:52,387 --> 00:24:53,353
Sorry, Mike.

595
00:24:53,388 --> 00:24:54,458
-Oh, boy.
-We had escape pods.

596
00:24:54,493 --> 00:24:55,459
We didn't use them.

597
00:24:55,494 --> 00:24:56,598
No big deal.
-Wait, wait, wait.

598
00:24:56,633 --> 00:24:57,979
Isn't there just one more?
-Oh, yeah.

599
00:24:58,013 --> 00:24:59,532
Gypsy has got it out.
She'll be along any second now.

600
00:24:59,567 --> 00:25:01,500
-Ah. 
-For England.

601
00:25:01,534 --> 00:25:02,846
And the Queen!
-All right!

602
00:25:02,880 --> 00:25:05,814
Go for Gyps!
-We'll be right back.

603
00:25:05,849 --> 00:25:10,750
♪♪

604
00:25:13,166 --> 00:25:15,755
-Oh, that was fun.
-Hi, Scott Devers.

605
00:25:15,790 --> 00:25:17,516
-Dave Ryder.
-Pleased to meet you.

606
00:25:17,550 --> 00:25:21,312
-Shall we do it?
-Well, this is sudden.

607
00:25:21,347 --> 00:25:22,417
-Lieutenant?
-Sir?

608
00:25:22,451 --> 00:25:24,315
-Please file this.
-Certainly, sir.

609
00:25:24,350 --> 00:25:25,903
-Thank you.
-Do you know where I can get

610
00:25:25,938 --> 00:25:27,353
some Zubaz, man?

611
00:25:27,387 --> 00:25:28,665
-Commander Jansen.

612
00:25:28,699 --> 00:25:31,322
-Well, welcome aboard,
Mr. Ryder.

613
00:25:31,357 --> 00:25:33,980
You've met our captain, Devers.
Sit down, son.

614
00:25:34,015 --> 00:25:35,395
-Thank you, sir.
-Oh, Ryder,

615
00:25:35,430 --> 00:25:38,157
could I have
your space status card, please?

616
00:25:38,191 --> 00:25:40,297
Thank you.
-Sorry it's so moist.

617
00:25:42,886 --> 00:25:46,406
-You've got mail.

618
00:25:46,441 --> 00:25:49,202
-Well, there we have it.
Any questions, Mr. Ryder?

619
00:25:49,237 --> 00:25:51,515
-Sir, I'd like to see a video
of the crash if I may.

620
00:25:51,550 --> 00:25:53,172
-Good idea.
Come this way.

621
00:25:53,206 --> 00:25:55,761
-I'll show you where my elves
are working day and night.

622
00:25:55,795 --> 00:25:57,763
-Take a chair.
-And ram it.

623
00:26:00,766 --> 00:26:02,112
-Lieutenant?
-Yes, sir?

624
00:26:02,146 --> 00:26:04,528
-Could you punch up a video
of the crash, please?

625
00:26:04,563 --> 00:26:05,598
-Yes, sir.

626
00:26:05,633 --> 00:26:08,497
-On our computer. 
-Disaster analysis.

627
00:26:08,532 --> 00:26:10,845
Guidance system engaged.
-Oi.

628
00:26:10,879 --> 00:26:12,605
-You are now on 
theSouthern Sun's

629
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:13,744
guidance control system.
-Ho.

630
00:26:13,779 --> 00:26:16,057
-Over. 
Pilot control released.

631
00:26:16,091 --> 00:26:19,439
Warning: critical power loss.

632
00:26:19,474 --> 00:26:22,373
-We now switch live
to Spencer's Gifts.

633
00:26:24,859 --> 00:26:26,964
-Hey, Macarena.

634
00:26:30,485 --> 00:26:32,245
-Ay.

635
00:26:32,280 --> 00:26:34,972
♪♪

636
00:26:35,007 --> 00:26:37,112
-It's a Wicca Tupperware party.

637
00:26:37,147 --> 00:26:41,530
♪♪

638
00:26:41,565 --> 00:26:43,256
-Steve called?

639
00:26:43,291 --> 00:26:46,294
My poultice.

640
00:26:46,328 --> 00:26:48,883
-Oh, I've got this itch
right on my leg there.

641
00:26:48,917 --> 00:26:50,609
Ah.

642
00:26:50,643 --> 00:26:53,059
Look familiar, m--
uh, what am I saying?

643
00:26:53,094 --> 00:26:56,304
No way.
-Hey.

644
00:26:56,338 --> 00:26:58,202
Damn Swedish ergonomic chairs.

645
00:26:58,237 --> 00:27:01,412
How do you sit
comfortably on these?

646
00:27:01,447 --> 00:27:02,655
Oh.

647
00:27:02,690 --> 00:27:03,863
-Eh, get a bunch
of women together,

648
00:27:03,898 --> 00:27:06,141
it's either witchery
or a wedding shower.

649
00:27:06,176 --> 00:27:08,488
That's what I say.

650
00:27:08,523 --> 00:27:11,077
-Mother Angelica aerobics.

651
00:27:11,112 --> 00:27:14,287
-I heard that.

652
00:27:16,186 --> 00:27:20,052
-Oh, I better get the phone,
you guys.

653
00:27:22,226 --> 00:27:24,021
-You've received our message.

654
00:27:24,056 --> 00:27:26,714
I'm glad you've come. 
We've been waiting for you.

655
00:27:26,748 --> 00:27:29,095
-Hey, you, the Bellerians
are off-limits.

656
00:27:29,130 --> 00:27:30,890
-You've never heard of
the "getting some" clause?

657
00:27:30,925 --> 00:27:32,064
-I was...

658
00:27:32,098 --> 00:27:34,238
-Well, there we are, gentlemen.

659
00:27:34,273 --> 00:27:36,102
-Tell me, Dave...
-Slab bulkhead.

660
00:27:36,137 --> 00:27:40,003
-Your Viperwas equipped with
a new high-density de-atomizer

661
00:27:40,037 --> 00:27:41,729
escape system, right?

662
00:27:41,763 --> 00:27:42,971
-Yes, commander.

663
00:27:43,006 --> 00:27:45,456
Right now, it only works
over very short distances,

664
00:27:45,491 --> 00:27:48,183
but who knows what the future
potential of it could be.

665
00:27:48,218 --> 00:27:50,116
-What about the professor?
-What's his max?

666
00:27:50,151 --> 00:27:52,498
-Commander, I'm sorry
about the professor.

667
00:27:52,532 --> 00:27:54,327
There's nothing
I could have done.

668
00:27:54,362 --> 00:27:57,399
The system is only hooked up
to the Viperpilot.

669
00:27:57,434 --> 00:27:58,711
-Don't blame yourself, son.

670
00:27:58,746 --> 00:28:00,402
-It's not your fault
you're a chunk-head.

671
00:28:00,437 --> 00:28:02,025
-You're lucky you're alive.

672
00:28:02,059 --> 00:28:04,613
You're lucky you saved yourself.

673
00:28:04,648 --> 00:28:06,167
-I can't breathe.

674
00:28:06,201 --> 00:28:10,550
-Lea, you had us all worried.

675
00:28:10,585 --> 00:28:12,207
Please, next time
there's a fire,

676
00:28:12,242 --> 00:28:14,485
leave it to damage control.

677
00:28:14,520 --> 00:28:16,315
You okay?
-Okay?

678
00:28:16,349 --> 00:28:19,387
Next time, young lady,
you stay out of the way.

679
00:28:19,421 --> 00:28:20,560
-Dad, I was there!
-Oh.

680
00:28:20,595 --> 00:28:21,734
-The pilot chickened out.

681
00:28:21,769 --> 00:28:24,703
Otherwise, Spooner
would be alive right now!

682
00:28:24,737 --> 00:28:28,189
-David Ryder, I want you
to meet my daughter, Lea.

683
00:28:28,223 --> 00:28:29,777
-We're about the same age.

684
00:28:29,811 --> 00:28:31,744
-Professor never had a chance.

685
00:28:31,779 --> 00:28:33,504
There's nothing I could
have done to prevent it.

686
00:28:33,539 --> 00:28:36,922
-Oh, so you left him to die...
-Lea, stop it!

687
00:28:36,956 --> 00:28:38,958
-He ejected, and he's alive!

688
00:28:38,993 --> 00:28:40,028
-Listen, lady!

689
00:28:40,063 --> 00:28:41,685
-Doctor!
-Doctor!

690
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:42,928
-Dr. Lady!

691
00:28:42,962 --> 00:28:44,723
-I don't have to justify
my actions to you,

692
00:28:44,757 --> 00:28:48,105
but since you're asking,
that explosion cut the power,

693
00:28:48,140 --> 00:28:51,419
and there wasn't time to go overthe auxiliary backup system.

694
00:28:51,453 --> 00:28:54,215
I had to eject.
I had no other choice.

695
00:28:54,249 --> 00:28:57,770
-That's, "Doctor, I had
no other choice."

696
00:28:57,805 --> 00:29:00,083
-Commander, Captain, excuse me.

697
00:29:00,117 --> 00:29:01,774
I have to file my report.

698
00:29:01,809 --> 00:29:05,709
-Coach will totally ream me
if I don't file my report.

699
00:29:05,744 --> 00:29:07,400
-Lea...

700
00:29:07,435 --> 00:29:10,024
-You're getting a lump of coal.

701
00:29:12,474 --> 00:29:16,030
-I like playing with the knobs.

702
00:29:16,064 --> 00:29:18,584
-All you can eat me tonight.
-Excuse me, sir.

703
00:29:18,618 --> 00:29:20,897
I think you'll find
this interesting.

704
00:29:20,931 --> 00:29:22,484
-Yes, what is it?

705
00:29:22,519 --> 00:29:23,865
-It's an inventory of all
the explosives

706
00:29:23,900 --> 00:29:26,799
under our control.

707
00:29:26,834 --> 00:29:28,939
-Hey, one of the new monkeys.

708
00:29:31,631 --> 00:29:35,325
-Oh, Gopher, are you lost?

709
00:29:35,359 --> 00:29:37,396
-He's calling to check
on his gender.

710
00:29:37,430 --> 00:29:40,779
-Uh, give me an audio/videolinkup, bridge to console seven.

711
00:29:40,813 --> 00:29:42,194
Please hurry.

712
00:29:42,228 --> 00:29:43,712
-There's something coming
through on the voice monitor

713
00:29:43,747 --> 00:29:44,990
from the engine-room area.

714
00:29:45,024 --> 00:29:46,957
-Wow.
-Put it through on five.

715
00:29:48,994 --> 00:29:50,961
-The electrolysis is working.

716
00:29:53,446 --> 00:29:56,760
-Those Formica monitors
don't have a lot of resolution.

717
00:29:56,795 --> 00:29:59,625
-My name is 
Flight Lieutenant Lemont.

718
00:29:59,659 --> 00:30:01,730
-Well, according to my printout
from the supply store's

719
00:30:01,765 --> 00:30:03,629
inventory,
we're definitely short

720
00:30:03,663 --> 00:30:05,838
on conventional
ballistic explosive.

721
00:30:05,873 --> 00:30:07,633
I mean, I double-checked.

722
00:30:07,667 --> 00:30:09,393
Somebody with direct 
online access

723
00:30:09,428 --> 00:30:10,739
to central 
has been transferring...

724
00:30:10,774 --> 00:30:12,776
-Oh, wait, whoops. 
-...a large amount

725
00:30:12,811 --> 00:30:15,227
of explosives and then simply 
covering the requisition.

726
00:30:15,261 --> 00:30:17,367
I wouldn't have found out about it unless central asked me

727
00:30:17,401 --> 00:30:19,231
to confirm acceptance 
of 100 units

728
00:30:19,265 --> 00:30:21,785
of chemo-plastic 
and atomic compound.

729
00:30:21,820 --> 00:30:23,269
I mean, that's crazy.

730
00:30:23,304 --> 00:30:24,546
Can you imagine that amount 
of explosives lying around

731
00:30:24,581 --> 00:30:25,616
the ship's engine room?

732
00:30:25,651 --> 00:30:27,584
-Come on, skull.
Pop out of my skin.

733
00:30:27,618 --> 00:30:30,000
-Anyway, I think I've traced 
who it is.

734
00:30:30,035 --> 00:30:31,622
-Who in the hell
is he talking to?

735
00:30:31,657 --> 00:30:33,383
Put it through to the bridge.

736
00:30:33,417 --> 00:30:35,350
-I want to speak to somebody 
from command, please.

737
00:30:35,385 --> 00:30:36,696
-Excuse me, Al Lewis.

738
00:30:36,731 --> 00:30:38,802
-Okay, for the sake of 
security,

739
00:30:38,837 --> 00:30:40,148
I think it would be better 
if you came up here

740
00:30:40,183 --> 00:30:42,702
and asked for me, 
Lieutenant Lemont.

741
00:30:42,737 --> 00:30:44,635
-Send a couple of menover there to stop that engineer

742
00:30:44,670 --> 00:30:46,396
before he gets to the bridge --

743
00:30:46,430 --> 00:30:48,225
unless I get to him first.

744
00:30:48,260 --> 00:30:51,056
-Time me.
Go ahead.

745
00:30:51,090 --> 00:30:52,436
Well, I think I just
have to report this.

746
00:30:52,471 --> 00:30:53,575
I mean, I really thought
about it,

747
00:30:53,610 --> 00:30:54,645
and I think I really
have to report this.

748
00:30:54,680 --> 00:30:56,164
I really, really
have to report it.

749
00:30:56,199 --> 00:30:58,166
-Herbie, the misfit elf.

750
00:31:00,272 --> 00:31:04,207
-Looks like Billie Jean King.

751
00:31:04,241 --> 00:31:07,417
-Oh, no, snowmobilers!

752
00:31:07,451 --> 00:31:10,420
-I've seen this before,
compulsory Splatball.

753
00:31:12,871 --> 00:31:15,114
-You know, if we pretend
we know what's going on,

754
00:31:15,149 --> 00:31:16,460
this is actually
kind of exciting.

755
